From e5f6bcecd90500e0a509e0093ed74c42af263241 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CHIBiNGA-1 <chibinga28@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 03:33:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add Privacy Policy and Terms of Service pages
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

frontend/app/privacy/page.tsx and frontend/app/terms/page.tsx — needed
for Google's OAuth consent screen branding (Application home page,
Privacy policy, Terms of service links), which is what actually gets
the consent screen to show "KraTte" instead of the raw Supabase project
domain.

Content reflects what the app actually does — Supabase for auth/data,
Gemini for reading WhatsApp photos/text, Meta's WhatsApp Business
Platform, manual MoMo payment verification, no ad sales — rather than
generic boilerplate, since Google's verification checks that the
policy matches the app's real data use. Both pages have a placeholder
contact email (PUT-YOUR-CONTACT-EMAIL-HERE) that needs a real address
before publishing.

Once pushed, the URLs are:
https://kratte.vercel.app/privacy
https://kratte.vercel.app/terms

Not legal advice — worth a lawyer's look before wide public launch,
but accurately describes the current data flows for now.

Verified: npm run build compiles cleanly, both routes render as static
pages.
---
 frontend/app/privacy/page.tsx | 123 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 frontend/app/terms/page.tsx   | 112 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 235 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 frontend/app/privacy/page.tsx
 create mode 100644 frontend/app/terms/page.tsx

